  "content": {
    "id": "v2-978ba-p65-practice-slot-6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "A quokka population on an island follows $P(t)=\\dfrac{C}{1+Ae^{-kt}}$, where $t$ is in years. Initially the population is $10\\%$ of the carrying capacity $C$, and after 3 years it is $50\\%$ of $C$. After how many years does it reach $90\\%$ of $C$?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "6 years.",
      "worked": "Using $P(0)=0.1C$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{C}{1+A}&=0.1C\\\\1+A&=10\\\\A&=9.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $P(3)=0.5C$:\n$$\\begin{align*}1+9e^{-3k}&=2\\\\e^{-3k}&=\\frac19.\\end{align*}$$\nFor $P(t)=0.9C$:\n$$\\begin{align*}1+9e^{-kt}&=\\frac{10}{9}\\\\e^{-kt}&=\\frac1{81}=\\left(\\frac19\\right)^2=e^{-6k}\\\\t&=6.\\end{align*}$$\nThe population reaches $90\\%$ of $C$ after 6 years.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
  },
